+P4 — matched A/B acceptance specification (NO execution authorized here)
+PROVISIONAL — NOT FOR PUBLIC HEADLINE
+Base: 15ded2f3add148c4db3c900cba7de878238f53bc + ordered patch hashes.
+Classification: local-only experiment specification; no measured kernel claim.
+Capture status: spec only, changes no runtime; D3 HOLD before ANY image build.
+
+Question and kill gates
+Does real 3bpw K3 ESIMD retain quality and deliver >=10% faster corrected C1
+p512/g128 token rate than the 4bpw ESIMD incumbent, without >5% prefill regression?
+Quality is a standing kill gate, not a tradeoff: repeat the trial's exact-answer
+6/6 battery twice (including code_execution=14), spec canary, and deterministic
+replay; rerun the 10 host-executed tasks (require >=9/10 with no regression on the
+exact-answer cases). Inspect every failure before timing. The earlier Triton
+quality GO does not establish correctness of these new kernels.
+
+Inherited context, not matched acceptance data
+- Trial evidence: ~/B70-DOCS/results/2026/09/b70-3bpw-trial-20260929/.
+  K3 Triton p512/g128 n=3 diagnostic corrected-token-rate glance = 10.25 tok/s,
+  configured cap 230 W; ledger RL-094 reports 147.9 W draw. This does not establish
+  a general power-scaling law. MTP3 marginal survivals 0.882/0.811/0.337,
+  mean accepted length 3.03; diagnostics only, not the selection objective.
+- Incumbent reference supplied by operator: 63.25 tok/s, ESIMD 4bpw corrected
+  metric. Exact statistic/build/cache/duration coordinates must be recovered from
+  ~/B70-DOCS/results/2026/09/b70-probe1-exl3-rate-20260929/ before use;
+  unspecified coordinates remain UNKNOWN, not inferred from a filename.
+- Arithmetic planning threshold only: 1.10*63.25 = 69.575 tok/s. No current
